7112b6b29bcf, C-14444dd6b10a) or hit geometry or extrapolation failures (C-05edbf22eaa2, C-3136d3bd2588). With one evaluation left, the safest way to gain hypervolume is to fill a gap on the ridge. The largest visible gap in gamma is between -1.68 and -1.9317 (C-d67052cfd2f9 to C-33a892b93afd).\",\"evidence\":[\"C-d67052cfd2f9: gamma -1.68 gives flux 230760 W/m2 and T 414.92 K.\",\"C-33a892b93afd: gamma -1.9317 gives flux 236070 W/m2 and T 411.00 K.\",\"C-e9d1bc94c0c6 to C-d67052cfd2f9 to C-33a892b93afd: flux and T are nearly linear in gamma, at roughly 20-21k W/m2 per deg and 16 K per deg, so interpolation is reliable.\",\"Every evaluated gamma from -1.5 to -3.5703 at (3.3852, 1.2, 70) is feasible, so a mid-range gamma should keep all margins positive; the mass-fraction margin appears independent of gamma.\",\"C-956957ec60d4, C-7112b6b29bcf, C-14444dd6b10a: reducing bluntness violates the mass fraction, so the corner is the right place to stay.\",\"C-c461ce8af13c: the max_g margin at gamma -3.5703 is only 1.9e-5, so the steep end is exhausted.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak g is set almost entirely by gamma, so the g limit fixes the steep end. Mass fraction fixes D. Shallower gamma lowers peak flux because entry is at lower density for longer, but lengthens the heat pulse and raises the bondline T. That gives a monotone, nearly linear trade-off along gamma. A point at gamma of about -1.8 sits in the widest visible gap between neighbours and adds a small hypervolume increment. It uses only the existing, verified geometry, so there is no risk of geometry or extrapolation failure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The hypervolume gain is small, about 1e-5 in normalised terms. I have not seen the full 81-point front, so an unseen point may already fill this gap. The flux and T values are linear interpolations from the data, not from a physical model.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-d67052cfd2f9\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the widest visible gap on the ridge between gamma -1.68 and -1.9317, keeping the verified corner geometry (D 3.3852, bluntness 1.2, cone 70) so the design is feasible and buildable.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":233200.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"It is the last evaluation. It is a near-certain feasible point that adds a small but positive hypervolume increment by densifying the shallow-gamma part of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":20623,"type":"result","duration_ms":32285,"uuid":"ff7c8ffb-e30d-4974-98f3-f3f15c1d23d4","ttft_stream_ms":2358,"time_to_request_ms":197,"first_content_frame_ms":2359,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
